## Context

Reported from padme, 2026-10-30. `close-and-clean.sh --phase before-exit` on a
merged ticket worktree ended with `roar: RESULT: findings (exit 1)`. The cause
is printed on its own earlier line (for example `PREFLIGHT: DIRTY …`,
`skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh:206`), but the session filtered the output to
the `CLOSE|CLAIMS|RESULT` lines and lost it; the worktree was then removed
cleanly by `after-exit` and the finding could no longer be recovered. Low
severity: nothing was lost but the explanation. Filed at the author's request.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The `RESULT: findings` line names the checks that fired (for example
      `RESULT: findings (exit 1): PREFLIGHT`), so the one-line verdict is
      self-sufficient
- [ ] Test covers a dirty-preflight run and asserts the named check on the RESULT line
